  "_notes": [
    "Times on the wire are engine frames as f64 (JS converts native ctx seconds with Engine.frameAt before encoding), except tau and duration, which stay in seconds.",
    "start.duration < 0 means none. node ids are issued by JS, unique per engine, never reused.",
    "param ids are the index into the node kind's param_specs() list, in the order the node declares them.",
    "message bytes for processors (genus, strobe_signal) are the processor's own encoding, documented in its Rust file and mirrored in nodes.js.",
    "A record's byteLength is a u16, so one record is at most 65,535 bytes: a curve of about 16,370 values, a message of about 65,520 bytes. The app's curves and chirp tables fit with room to spare; an event too long to fit is not sent.",
    "log(node, code, value) is the stage telling the page something it should know (enums.log_code). cycle_cut: at the last change of connections, `value` nodes sat in a cycle with no DelayNode and were silenced, the first of them `node`; it is sent when that changes, and once more with value 0 when the cycle is gone."
  ],
  "processor_messages": {
    "_": "Processor port messages travel as `message` command bytes and `port` event bytes, little-endian, no padding: a u32 type, then the fields. Times named *_frame are engine frames (JS converts native ctx seconds with Engine.frameAt); other times are seconds.",
